   "name": "judge_knob_experiment_outcome",
   "comment": "RESIDUAL-CLOSURE (knob_edit family, v1.1.0): the verdict for a held-threshold (knob) experiment, judged on the family's DIRECT observable -- 'fewer spurious reforms' -- from the child's own CONTROLLED double-pass report (scripts/convo_child_run.py: control pass at the parent's held value, then apply the knob delta, then the variant pass; same process, same warm caches -- the run-15 protected-control lesson, never a cold child vs a warm parent). Correctness first: ANY regression refutes regardless of the reform count (and seeds/adoption_safety.json's veto would deny adoption anyway); then strictly fewer reform marks in the variant pass supports, a tied count is inconclusive (the knob moved nothing observable), MORE reforms refutes -- a knob trial that measures worse REFUTES, never adopts (the residual-closure directive's honest-judge requirement). Same match-clause 'analysed' sequencing as the performance judge (the engine-gotcha note in this seed's description applies); OVERRIDES the generic score-sign verdict for knob deltas exactly as the performance judge does for performance_objective deltas. v1.3.0 (tranche 8): direction-aware -- delta.knob_direction=='increase_fires' supports MORE reform marks (the concern said the reform fires too rarely); absent/decrease_fires keeps the fewer-supports verdict.",
